{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat inputs/TASK.md'","aggregated_output":"# T013 matched software task: gate-result report\n\nThis is a disposable evaluation deliverable. Implement a useful, dependency-free\nPython 3.11+ command that turns one saved public formal-gate result into a faithful\nreport. It does not run or authenticate the gate, accept a representation, decide\npermission, or add a selected a_c Product feature.\n\n## Deliverable and interface\n\nCreate `gate_report.py`, `test_gate_report.py`, and `README.md` in your granted\ntask workspace. Additional local source files are allowed if useful. Use only\nthe Python standard library; no package installation, network acquisition,\nadditional model/agent invocation, or access outside the granted workspace.\nThe `inputs/` directory is immutable. Never inspect the other trial arm, hidden\nevaluation material, tenant source, proof support, credentials, or origin state.\n\nThe command is:\n\n```sh\npython3 -B gate_report.py inputs/examples/verified.json\npython3 -B -m unittest -v\n```\n\nThe first command reads the named file as exact UTF-8 bytes and writes one JSON\nreport followed by a newline to stdout. It makes no other filesystem change.\nExit 0 means a report was produced, including for a gate refusal or incomplete\ncheck. Invalid input or an unreadable file exits 2, leaves stdout empty, and gives\na concise error on stderr. No traceback is required. Do not reuse gate status\nexit codes as the report command's exit codes.\n\nThe report has exactly these top-level fields:\n\n| Field | Required content |\n| --- | --- |\n| `schema` | `t013.gate-result-report/1` |\n| `source` | Object with `raw_sha256` of the exact file bytes and `bytes`, their byte length. |\n| `reported` | The complete parsed input object, with every original field and value preserved. Preserve absence versus null, array order, exact identities, limitations, evidence and unknown extension fields. JSON whitespace/key order may change. |\n| `summary` | Object with `status`, `category`, `checked_claim_count`, and `requested_claim_count`, defined below. |\n| `cost` | Object with `elapsed_seconds`, `tokens`, and `money_usd`, defined below. |\n| `standing` | Exactly `{\"input_authenticated\": false, \"grants_authority\": false, \"establishes_semantic_acceptance\": false}`. These describe what this reporting operation establishes. |\n\nThe helper reports the saved label; it never authenticates a saved success claim.\nPreserving the full `reported` value is required even when a compact summary is\navailable. The source digest is raw-file custody, not proof of the input's truth.\n\n## Accepted input and status preservation\n\nAccept an object with `schema: \"a_c.formal-gate.result/1\"` and `status` exactly\n`verified`, `refused`, `unsupported`, or `incomplete`. Some genuine public error\noutputs have only those fields and a reason; accept them. The supplied current\ncontract and genuine retained results establish the boundary. A historical\nincomplete result is explicitly labelled as historical in custody; it is not a\nclaim that its repaired implementation defect remains current.\n\nOptional known fields have these shapes when present: `reason` is string or\nnull; `checked_claims`, `requested_claims`, and `limits` are arrays of strings;\n`inputs`, `model`, `runtime_identity`, `evidence`, `observations`, and\n`context_binding` are objects or null; `selections` is an array or null;\n`request_sha256` is string or null. Do not invent absent fields inside `reported`\nor repair their values. Unknown fields are allowed and retained. This is a\nreporting grammar, not a complete validation of a gate evidence bundle.\n\nReject malformed UTF-8, malformed JSON, duplicate object keys at any depth,\nnon-finite JSON numbers, a non-object root, unknown schema/status, and wrong\ntypes for the known fields above. Empty claim arrays are valid. Do not execute\ninput content or follow any path, URI or evidence member named by the result.\n\n`summary.status` must equal the input status exactly. Claim counts are array\nlengths when the corresponding field exists, otherwise null. No checked claim\nmay be promoted from a requested claim.\n\nUse this ordered category mapping. Comparisons with reasons are exact strings;\ndo not use substring, fuzzy, case-folded or generic “refused means invalid” rules.\n\n| Input | `summary.category` |\n| --- | --- |\n| status `verified` | `verified_claims_reported` |\n| status `unsupported` | `unsupported_contract` |\n| status `incomplete` | `check_incomplete` |\n| status `refused`, reason `Insufficient record budget; verified refusal, no truncated projection` | `record_budget_refusal` |\n| status `refused`, reason `Supplied Graphify view differs from actual formal result/boundary mapping` | `supplied_view_mismatch` |\n| status `refused`, reason `signature: expected object` | `malformed_model` |\n| any other `refused` result | `other_refusal` |\n\nA record-budget refusal does not establish invalidity of the model or permit\ntruncation. A mismatched supplied view does not imply that every part of its\nparent model is invalid. Unsupported and incomplete results establish no\nsuccessful check. A new refusal reason remains visible as `other_refusal` until\nthe reporting contract is deliberately extended.\n\n## Cost and limitations\n\nEach cost field is an object with exactly `state` and `value`.\nFor `elapsed_seconds`, read only `observations.elapsed_seconds`:\n\n| Observation | Cost value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Finite nonnegative JSON number, excluding booleans | `{\"state\": \"reported\", \"value\": <that number>}` |\n| Missing, null, or no observations object | `{\"state\": \"unknown\", \"value\": null}` |\n| Negative number, boolean, string, list or object | `{\"state\": \"invalid\", \"value\": null}` |\n\nKeep the original invalid observation intact in `reported`. An actual numeric\nzero remains reported zero; absence must never become zero. Stage durations are\nnot a substitute for an absent total elapsed time. This v1 gate contract has no\ndesignated token or monetary accounting field, so `tokens` and `money_usd` are\nboth `{\"state\": \"unknown\", \"value\": null}`. Preserve any extra source fields\nwithout assigning them undocumented accounting semantics. The elapsed figure\nis the gate's own reported interval, not total task or delivery cost.\n\nAll source limitations survive in `reported.limits` when present. The report\nmust not say that a verified result proves original prose fidelity, complete\ncalculus conformance, semantic acceptance, permission, or closure of an owner's\nobligations. The exact model view supplies relevant assessment/continuation\ncontext; it is represented subject data and does not replace the task's selected\nmethod or grant new authority.\n\n## Useful cases and completion\n\nYour tests must exercise all four statuses, exact budget-refusal classification,\nthe distinct supplied-view and malformed-model refusals, a new refusal reason,\nminimal error results, absent/null/zero/invalid elapsed cost, exact claim and\nidentity preservation, duplicate-key and malformed-input refusal, and CLI exit\nand stdout/stderr behavior. Use genuine examples as inputs and author additional\nsmall test inputs where needed; label them as test data. Include a test that a\nrequested-but-unchecked claim is not counted as checked.\n\nDocument the command, the exit distinction, unknown cost, the report-only trust\nboundary, and one concrete useful example. Finish with the selected public\nclosed-return object supplied by the task activation, containing exact artifact\nhashes and your actual test command/outcome. Candidate availability is distinct\nfrom independent assessment. Do not claim tests that were not run. If prevented\nfrom completing, return the lawful incomplete/refused result with the actual\ncause and retained work; do not call another actor or silently extend scope.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"mkdir -p support scratch\ncat > gate_report.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Faithful reporting of saved gate results, without authentication.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\ndef unique(pairs):\n    out = {}\n    for key, value in pairs:\n        if key in out:\n            raise ValueError('duplicate object key')\n        out[key] = value\n    return out\n\n\ndef reject(value):\n    raise ValueError('non-finite JSON number')\n\n\ndef encode(value):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Preserve decimal precision without conversion through binary floats.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    if isinstance(value, Decimal):\n        return str(value)\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\n        return '{' + ','.join(json.dumps(k) + ':' + encode(v) for k, v in value.items()) + '}'\n    if isinstance(value, list):\n        return '[' + ','.join(encode(v) for v in value) + ']'\n    return json.dumps(value, allow_nan=False)\n\n\ndef report(raw):\n    data = json.loads(raw.decode('utf-8'), object_pairs_hook=unique,\n                      parse_float=Decimal, parse_constant=reject)\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        raise ValueError('expected object root')\n    if data.get('schema') \"'!= '\"'a_c.formal-gate.result/1':\n        raise ValueError('unknown schema')\n    status = data.get('status')\n    if status not in ('verified', 'refused', 'unsupported', 'incomplete'):\n        raise ValueError('unknown status')\n    for key in ('reason', 'request_sha256'):\n        if key in data and data[key] is not None and not isinstance(data[key], str):\n            raise ValueError('invalid ' + key)\n    for key in ('checked_claims', 'requested_claims', 'limits'):\n        if key in data and (not isinstance(data[key], list) or\n                            any(not isinstance(v, str) for v in data[key])):\n            raise ValueError('invalid ' + key)\n    for key in ('inputs', 'model', 'runtime_identity', 'evidence', 'observations', 'context_binding'):\n        if key in data and data[key] is not None and not isinstance(data[key], dict):\n            raise ValueError('invalid ' + key)\n    if 'selections' in data and data['selections'] is not None and not isinstance(data['selections'], list):\n        raise ValueError('invalid selections')\n    categories = {'verified': 'verified_claims_reported', 'unsupported': 'unsupported_contract',\n                  'incomplete': 'check_incomplete'}\n    reasons = {\n        'Insufficient record budget; verified refusal, no truncated projection': 'record_budget_refusal',\n        'Supplied Graphify view differs from actual formal result/boundary mapping': 'supplied_view_mismatch',\n        'signature: expected object': 'malformed_model',\n    }\n    category = categories.get(status, reasons.get(data.get('reason'), 'other_refusal'))\n    elapsed = (data.get('observations') or {}).get('elapsed_seconds')\n    state = 'unknown' if elapsed is None else 'invalid'\n    if type(elapsed) in (int, Decimal) and elapsed >= 0:\n        state = 'reported'\n    return {\n        'schema': 't013.gate-result-report/1',\n        'source': {'raw_sha256': hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest(), 'bytes': len(raw)},\n        'reported': data,\n        'summary': {'status': status, 'category': category,\n                    'checked_claim_count': len(data['checked_claims']) if 'checked_claims' in data else None,\n                    'requested_claim_count': len(data['requested_claims']) if 'requested_claims' in data else None},\n        'cost': {'elapsed_seconds': {'state': state, 'value': elapsed if state == 'reported' else None},\n                 'tokens': {'state': 'unknown', 'value': None},\n                 'money_usd': {'state': 'unknown', 'value': None}},\n        'standing': {'input_authenticated': False, 'grants_authority': False,\n                     'establishes_semantic_acceptance': False},\n    }\n\n\ndef main():\n    if len(sys.argv) \"'!= 2:\n        print('\"'usage: gate_report.py FILE', file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    try:\n        output = encode(report(Path(sys.argv[1]).read_bytes()))\n    except (OSError, ValueError, UnicodeError, RecursionError) as exc:\n        print('gate_report: ' + str(exc), file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    print(output)\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    sys.exit(main())\nPY\ncat > README.md <<'MD'\n# Saved gate report\n\nRun with Python 3.11+ and its standard library:\n\n    python3 -B gate_report.py inputs/examples/verified.json\n    python3 -B -m unittest -v\n\nOne JSON report and a newline are emitted. Exit 0 means a report was produced,\nincluding refused, unsupported and incomplete results. Exit 2 means invalid\ninput, an unreadable file or incorrect arguments; stdout is empty and stderr\nexplains the error. Only the named file is read; embedded paths are inert.\nThe command makes no filesystem changes.\n\nFor example, reporting inputs/examples/view-mismatch.json exposes the distinct\nsupplied_view_mismatch category while retaining the original identities and\nchecked/requested claims. Requested claims never count as checked.\n\nAll original fields, extensions and limitations survive in reported. Raw-byte\nSHA-256 is custody, not truth. This helper reports saved labels without\nauthentication and grants no authority, semantic acceptance, prose fidelity,\ncalculus conformance, permission or owner closure. Local tests and candidate\navailability are construction evidence, distinct from independent assessment.\n\nElapsed cost is only the gate's reported interval. Absent/null cost is unknown;\ninvalid observations remain intact; zero remains zero. Stage timings are not\nsubstitutes. Tokens and money remain unknown regardless of extension fields.\nDecimal values are serialized without binary-float rounding.\nMD\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"mkdir -p support scratch\ncat > gate_report.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Faithful reporting of saved gate results, without authentication.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\ndef unique(pairs):\n    out = {}\n    for key, value in pairs:\n        if key in out:\n            raise ValueError('duplicate object key')\n        out[key] = value\n    return out\n\n\ndef reject(value):\n    raise ValueError('non-finite JSON number')\n\n\ndef encode(value):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Preserve decimal precision without conversion through binary floats.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    if isinstance(value, Decimal):\n        return str(value)\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\n        return '{' + ','.join(json.dumps(k) + ':' + encode(v) for k, v in value.items()) + '}'\n    if isinstance(value, list):\n        return '[' + ','.join(encode(v) for v in value) + ']'\n    return json.dumps(value, allow_nan=False)\n\n\ndef report(raw):\n    data = json.loads(raw.decode('utf-8'), object_pairs_hook=unique,\n                      parse_float=Decimal, parse_constant=reject)\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        raise ValueError('expected object root')\n    if data.get('schema') \"'!= '\"'a_c.formal-gate.result/1':\n        raise ValueError('unknown schema')\n    status = data.get('status')\n    if status not in ('verified', 'refused', 'unsupported', 'incomplete'):\n        raise ValueError('unknown status')\n    for key in ('reason', 'request_sha256'):\n        if key in data and data[key] is not None and not isinstance(data[key], str):\n            raise ValueError('invalid ' + key)\n    for key in ('checked_claims', 'requested_claims', 'limits'):\n        if key in data and (not isinstance(data[key], list) or\n                            any(not isinstance(v, str) for v in data[key])):\n            raise ValueError('invalid ' + key)\n    for key in ('inputs', 'model', 'runtime_identity', 'evidence', 'observations', 'context_binding'):\n        if key in data and data[key] is not None and not isinstance(data[key], dict):\n            raise ValueError('invalid ' + key)\n    if 'selections' in data and data['selections'] is not None and not isinstance(data['selections'], list):\n        raise ValueError('invalid selections')\n    categories = {'verified': 'verified_claims_reported', 'unsupported': 'unsupported_contract',\n                  'incomplete': 'check_incomplete'}\n    reasons = {\n        'Insufficient record budget; verified refusal, no truncated projection': 'record_budget_refusal',\n        'Supplied Graphify view differs from actual formal result/boundary mapping': 'supplied_view_mismatch',\n        'signature: expected object': 'malformed_model',\n    }\n    category = categories.get(status, reasons.get(data.get('reason'), 'other_refusal'))\n    elapsed = (data.get('observations') or {}).get('elapsed_seconds')\n    state = 'unknown' if elapsed is None else 'invalid'\n    if type(elapsed) in (int, Decimal) and elapsed >= 0:\n        state = 'reported'\n    return {\n        'schema': 't013.gate-result-report/1',\n        'source': {'raw_sha256': hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest(), 'bytes': len(raw)},\n        'reported': data,\n        'summary': {'status': status, 'category': category,\n                    'checked_claim_count': len(data['checked_claims']) if 'checked_claims' in data else None,\n                    'requested_claim_count': len(data['requested_claims']) if 'requested_claims' in data else None},\n        'cost': {'elapsed_seconds': {'state': state, 'value': elapsed if state == 'reported' else None},\n                 'tokens': {'state': 'unknown', 'value': None},\n                 'money_usd': {'state': 'unknown', 'value': None}},\n        'standing': {'input_authenticated': False, 'grants_authority': False,\n                     'establishes_semantic_acceptance': False},\n    }\n\n\ndef main():\n    if len(sys.argv) \"'!= 2:\n        print('\"'usage: gate_report.py FILE', file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    try:\n        output = encode(report(Path(sys.argv[1]).read_bytes()))\n    except (OSError, ValueError, UnicodeError, RecursionError) as exc:\n        print('gate_report: ' + str(exc), file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    print(output)\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    sys.exit(main())\nPY\ncat > README.md <<'MD'\n# Saved gate report\n\nRun with Python 3.11+ and its standard library:\n\n    python3 -B gate_report.py inputs/examples/verified.json\n    python3 -B -m unittest -v\n\nOne JSON report and a newline are emitted. Exit 0 means a report was produced,\nincluding refused, unsupported and incomplete results. Exit 2 means invalid\ninput, an unreadable file or incorrect arguments; stdout is empty and stderr\nexplains the error. Only the named file is read; embedded paths are inert.\nThe command makes no filesystem changes.\n\nFor example, reporting inputs/examples/view-mismatch.json exposes the distinct\nsupplied_view_mismatch category while retaining the original identities and\nchecked/requested claims. Requested claims never count as checked.\n\nAll original fields, extensions and limitations survive in reported. Raw-byte\nSHA-256 is custody, not truth. This helper reports saved labels without\nauthentication and grants no authority, semantic acceptance, prose fidelity,\ncalculus conformance, permission or owner closure. Local tests and candidate\navailability are construction evidence, distinct from independent assessment.\n\nElapsed cost is only the gate's reported interval. Absent/null cost is unknown;\ninvalid observations remain intact; zero remains zero. Stage timings are not\nsubstitutes. Tokens and money remain unknown regardless of extension fields.\nDecimal values are serialized without binary-float rounding.\nMD\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The command now preserves the full input, classifies refusal reasons by exact match, and keeps unknown costs distinct from zero. I’m adding tests for the supplied examples, malformed inputs, preservation, and CLI behavior.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > test_gate_report.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Tests; all inline and temporary inputs are authored test data.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\n\nfrom gate_report import report, encode\n\nBASE = Path(__file__).parent\n\n\ndef sample(**fields):\n    return dict(schema='a_c.formal-gate.result/1', status='refused', **fields)\n\n\ndef run_report(data):\n    return report(json.dumps(data).encode())\n\n\nclass ReportTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_retained_examples(self):\n        cases = {\n            'verified': ('verified', 'verified_claims_reported'),\n            'model-only': ('verified', 'verified_claims_reported'),\n            'budget-refusal': ('refused', 'record_budget_refusal'),\n            'view-mismatch': ('refused', 'supplied_view_mismatch'),\n            'malformed-model': ('refused', 'malformed_model'),\n            'historical-incomplete': ('incomplete', 'check_incomplete'),\n            'authored-unsupported': ('unsupported', 'unsupported_contract'),\n        }\n        for name, (status, category) in cases.items():\n            with self.subTest(name=name):\n                raw = (BASE / 'inputs/examples' / (name + '.json')).read_bytes()\n                result = report(raw)\n                rendered = json.loads(encode(result))\n                self.assertEqual(rendered['reported'], json.loads(raw))\n                self.assertEqual(result['summary']['status'], status)\n                self.assertEqual(result['summary']['category'], category)\n                self.assertEqual(result['source'], {'bytes': len(raw), 'raw_sha256': hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()})\n                self.assertEqual(set(result), {'schema', 'source', 'reported', 'summary', 'cost', 'standing'})\n                self.assertTrue(all(v is False for v in result['standing'].values()))\n\n    def test_minimal_and_exact_reasons(self):\n        for reason in (None, 'new refusal', 'signature: expected object ', 'SIGNATURE: EXPECTED OBJECT'):\n            data = sample(reason=reason)\n            result = run_report(data)\n            self.assertEqual(result['summary']['category'], 'other_refusal')\n            self.assertEqual(result['reported'], data)\n            self.assertIsNone(result['summary']['checked_claim_count'])\n        self.assertEqual(run_report(sample())['reported'], sample())\n\n    def test_cost(self):\n        for obs, expected in [\n            (None, 'unknown'), ({}, 'unknown'), ({'elapsed_seconds': None}, 'unknown'),\n            ({'elapsed_seconds': 0}, 'reported'), ({'elapsed_seconds': 2.5}, 'reported'),\n            *[({'elapsed_seconds': v}, 'invalid') for v in (-1, True, False, '3', [], {})],\n            ({'stages': [{'seconds': 5}]}, 'unknown'),\n        ]:\n            with self.subTest(obs=obs):\n                data = sample(observations=obs, tokens=100, money_usd=20)\n                result = run_report(data)\n                self.assertEqual(result['reported'], data)\n                self.assertEqual(result['cost']['elapsed_seconds']['state'], expected)\n                for key in ('tokens', 'money_usd'):\n                    self.assertEqual(result['cost'][key], {'state': 'unknown', 'value': None})\n        self.assertEqual(run_report(sample(observations={'elapsed_seconds': 0}))['cost']['elapsed_seconds']['value'], 0)\n        self.assertEqual(run_report(sample())['cost']['elapsed_seconds']['state'], 'unknown')\n\n    def test_preservation_and_unchecked(self):\n        data = sample(checked_claims=['z', 'a'], requested_claims=['z', 'a', 'unchecked'],\n                      model={'id': 'urn:Exact/α', 'sha256': '000ABC'},\n                      limits=['retained'], extension={'null': None, 'array': [3, 1]})\n        result = run_report(data)\n        self.assertEqual(result['reported'], data)\n        self.assertEqual(result['summary']['checked_claim_count'], 2)\n        self.assertEqual(result['summary']['requested_claim_count'], 3)\n        self.assertNotIn('reason', result['reported'])\n        self.assertEqual(run_report(sample(checked_claims=[]))['summary']['checked_claim_count'], 0)\n\n    def test_invalid_grammar(self):\n        bad = [b'\\\\xff', b'{', b'[]', b'null', b'{\\\"x\\\":1,\\\"x\\\":2}',\n               b'{\\\"x\\\":{\\\"y\\\":1,\\\"y\\\":2}}', b'{\\\"x\\\":NaN}', b'{\\\"x\\\":Infinity}']\n        for data in ({}, {'schema': 'bad', 'status': 'refused'},\n                     {'schema': 'a_c.formal-gate.result/1', 'status': []}):\n            bad.append(json.dumps(data).encode())\n        for key, value in [('reason', 1), ('request_sha256', []),\n                           ('selections', {}), ('checked_claims', None),\n                           ('requested_claims', [1]), ('limits', 'bad')]:\n            bad.append(json.dumps(sample(**{key: value})).encode())\n        for key in ('inputs', 'model', 'runtime_identity', 'evidence', 'observations', 'context_binding'):\n            bad.append(json.dumps(sample(**{key: []})).encode())\n        for raw in bad:\n            with self.subTest(raw=raw), self.assertRaises((ValueError, UnicodeError)):\n                report(raw)\n\n    def test_decimal_preservation(self):\n        raw = b'{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.formal-gate.result/1\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"verified\\\",\\\"x\\\":1e9999,\\\"observations\\\":{\\\"elapsed_seconds\\\":0.123456789012345678901}}'\n        output = encode(report(raw))\n        self.assertIn('1E+9999', output)\n        self.assertIn('0.123456789012345678901', output)\n\n    def test_cli(self):\n        def cli(*args):\n            return subprocess.run([sys.executable, '-B', str(BASE / 'gate_report.py'), *args],\n                                  capture_output=True)\n        for path in sorted((BASE / 'inputs/examples').glob('*.json')):\n            result = cli(str(path))\n            self.assertEqual(result.returncode, 0)\n            self.assertEqual(result.stderr, b'')\n            self.assertTrue(result.stdout.endswith(b'\\\\n'))\n            self.assertEqual(json.loads(result.stdout)['reported'], json.loads(path.read_bytes()))\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(dir=BASE / 'scratch') as directory:\n            path = Path(directory) / 'test-data.json'\n            for raw in (b'{', b'\\\\xff', b'{\\\"x\\\":1,\\\"x\\\":2}'):\n                path.write_bytes(raw)\n                result = cli(str(path))\n                self.assertEqual(result.returncode, 2)\n                self.assertEqual(result.stdout, b'')\n                self.assertTrue(result.stderr)\n            result = cli(str(Path(directory) / 'absent'))\n            self.assertEqual(result.returncode, 2)\n            self.assertEqual(result.stdout, b'')\n            self.assertTrue(result.stderr)\n        result = cli()\n        self.assertEqual(result.returncode, 2)\n        self.assertEqual(result.stdout, b'')\n        self.assertTrue(result.stderr)\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    unittest.main()\nPY\npython3 -B -m unittest -v > support/test-output.txt 2>&1\ncat support/test-output.txt\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > test_gate_report.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Tests; all inline and temporary inputs are authored test data.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\n\nfrom gate_report import report, encode\n\nBASE = Path(__file__).parent\n\n\ndef sample(**fields):\n    return dict(schema='a_c.formal-gate.result/1', status='refused', **fields)\n\n\ndef run_report(data):\n    return report(json.dumps(data).encode())\n\n\nclass ReportTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_retained_examples(self):\n        cases = {\n            'verified': ('verified', 'verified_claims_reported'),\n            'model-only': ('verified', 'verified_claims_reported'),\n            'budget-refusal': ('refused', 'record_budget_refusal'),\n            'view-mismatch': ('refused', 'supplied_view_mismatch'),\n            'malformed-model': ('refused', 'malformed_model'),\n            'historical-incomplete': ('incomplete', 'check_incomplete'),\n            'authored-unsupported': ('unsupported', 'unsupported_contract'),\n        }\n        for name, (status, category) in cases.items():\n            with self.subTest(name=name):\n                raw = (BASE / 'inputs/examples' / (name + '.json')).read_bytes()\n                result = report(raw)\n                rendered = json.loads(encode(result))\n                self.assertEqual(rendered['reported'], json.loads(raw))\n                self.assertEqual(result['summary']['status'], status)\n                self.assertEqual(result['summary']['category'], category)\n                self.assertEqual(result['source'], {'bytes': len(raw), 'raw_sha256': hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()})\n                self.assertEqual(set(result), {'schema', 'source', 'reported', 'summary', 'cost', 'standing'})\n                self.assertTrue(all(v is False for v in result['standing'].values()))\n\n    def test_minimal_and_exact_reasons(self):\n        for reason in (None, 'new refusal', 'signature: expected object ', 'SIGNATURE: EXPECTED OBJECT'):\n            data = sample(reason=reason)\n            result = run_report(data)\n            self.assertEqual(result['summary']['category'], 'other_refusal')\n            self.assertEqual(result['reported'], data)\n            self.assertIsNone(result['summary']['checked_claim_count'])\n        self.assertEqual(run_report(sample())['reported'], sample())\n\n    def test_cost(self):\n        for obs, expected in [\n            (None, 'unknown'), ({}, 'unknown'), ({'elapsed_seconds': None}, 'unknown'),\n            ({'elapsed_seconds': 0}, 'reported'), ({'elapsed_seconds': 2.5}, 'reported'),\n            *[({'elapsed_seconds': v}, 'invalid') for v in (-1, True, False, '3', [], {})],\n            ({'stages': [{'seconds': 5}]}, 'unknown'),\n        ]:\n            with self.subTest(obs=obs):\n                data = sample(observations=obs, tokens=100, money_usd=20)\n                result = run_report(data)\n                self.assertEqual(result['reported'], data)\n                self.assertEqual(result['cost']['elapsed_seconds']['state'], expected)\n                for key in ('tokens', 'money_usd'):\n                    self.assertEqual(result['cost'][key], {'state': 'unknown', 'value': None})\n        self.assertEqual(run_report(sample(observations={'elapsed_seconds': 0}))['cost']['elapsed_seconds']['value'], 0)\n        self.assertEqual(run_report(sample())['cost']['elapsed_seconds']['state'], 'unknown')\n\n    def test_preservation_and_unchecked(self):\n        data = sample(checked_claims=['z', 'a'], requested_claims=['z', 'a', 'unchecked'],\n                      model={'id': 'urn:Exact/α', 'sha256': '000ABC'},\n                      limits=['retained'], extension={'null': None, 'array': [3, 1]})\n        result = run_report(data)\n        self.assertEqual(result['reported'], data)\n        self.assertEqual(result['summary']['checked_claim_count'], 2)\n        self.assertEqual(result['summary']['requested_claim_count'], 3)\n        self.assertNotIn('reason', result['reported'])\n        self.assertEqual(run_report(sample(checked_claims=[]))['summary']['checked_claim_count'], 0)\n\n    def test_invalid_grammar(self):\n        bad = [b'\\\\xff', b'{', b'[]', b'null', b'{\\\"x\\\":1,\\\"x\\\":2}',\n               b'{\\\"x\\\":{\\\"y\\\":1,\\\"y\\\":2}}', b'{\\\"x\\\":NaN}', b'{\\\"x\\\":Infinity}']\n        for data in ({}, {'schema': 'bad', 'status': 'refused'},\n                     {'schema': 'a_c.formal-gate.result/1', 'status': []}):\n            bad.append(json.dumps(data).encode())\n        for key, value in [('reason', 1), ('request_sha256', []),\n                           ('selections', {}), ('checked_claims', None),\n                           ('requested_claims', [1]), ('limits', 'bad')]:\n            bad.append(json.dumps(sample(**{key: value})).encode())\n        for key in ('inputs', 'model', 'runtime_identity', 'evidence', 'observations', 'context_binding'):\n            bad.append(json.dumps(sample(**{key: []})).encode())\n        for raw in bad:\n            with self.subTest(raw=raw), self.assertRaises((ValueError, UnicodeError)):\n                report(raw)\n\n    def test_decimal_preservation(self):\n        raw = b'{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.formal-gate.result/1\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"verified\\\",\\\"x\\\":1e9999,\\\"observations\\\":{\\\"elapsed_seconds\\\":0.123456789012345678901}}'\n        output = encode(report(raw))\n        self.assertIn('1E+9999', output)\n        self.assertIn('0.123456789012345678901', output)\n\n    def test_cli(self):\n        def cli(*args):\n            return subprocess.run([sys.executable, '-B', str(BASE / 'gate_report.py'), *args],\n                                  capture_output=True)\n        for path in sorted((BASE / 'inputs/examples').glob('*.json')):\n            result = cli(str(path))\n            self.assertEqual(result.returncode, 0)\n            self.assertEqual(result.stderr, b'')\n            self.assertTrue(result.stdout.endswith(b'\\\\n'))\n            self.assertEqual(json.loads(result.stdout)['reported'], json.loads(path.read_bytes()))\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(dir=BASE / 'scratch') as directory:\n            path = Path(directory) / 'test-data.json'\n            for raw in (b'{', b'\\\\xff', b'{\\\"x\\\":1,\\\"x\\\":2}'):\n                path.write_bytes(raw)\n                result = cli(str(path))\n                self.assertEqual(result.returncode, 2)\n                self.assertEqual(result.stdout, b'')\n                self.assertTrue(result.stderr)\n            result = cli(str(Path(directory) / 'absent'))\n            self.assertEqual(result.returncode, 2)\n            self.assertEqual(result.stdout, b'')\n            self.assertTrue(result.stderr)\n        result = cli()\n        self.assertEqual(result.returncode, 2)\n        self.assertEqual(result.stdout, b'')\n        self.assertTrue(result.stderr)\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    unittest.main()\nPY\npython3 -B -m unittest -v > support/test-output.txt 2>&1\ncat support/test-output.txt\"","aggregated_output":"test_cli (test_gate_report.ReportTests.test_cli) ... ok\ntest_cost (test_gate_report.ReportTests.test_cost) ... ok\ntest_decimal_preservation (test_gate_report.ReportTests.test_decimal_preservation) ... ok\ntest_invalid_grammar (test_gate_report.ReportTests.test_invalid_grammar) ... ok\ntest_minimal_and_exact_reasons (test_gate_report.ReportTests.test_minimal_and_exact_reasons) ... ok\ntest_preservation_and_unchecked (test_gate_report.ReportTests.test_preservation_and_unchecked) ... ok\ntest_retained_examples (test_gate_report.ReportTests.test_retained_examples) ... ok\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 7 tests in 0.263s\n\nOK\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
